      "semantic_links": [
        {
          "claim": "The native driver error is the concrete exported *github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql.MySQLError. Its Number uint16 and Message string are struct fields, not interface methods. Import the native driver under a distinct alias from trpc-database/mysql; use its concrete pointer type for errors.As. Never invent interface{Number uint16}, a nonexistent Number() method, or a local replacement struct.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "local_path": "sources/driver-errors.go-57.txt",
              "quote": "type MySQLError struct {"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/driver-errors.go-57.txt",
              "quote": "Number  uint16"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_transport.go-101.txt",
              "quote": "var mySQLError *mysql.MySQLError"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "claim": "The public Client.QueryRow(ctx,dest,query,args...) fills a destination []interface{} and returns error; it does NOT return *sql.Row like database/sql.DB.QueryRowContext. Client.Get is an available alternative for struct/scalar reads. The Client interface does not expose a GetDB() accessor: do not invent downcasts or native database/row adapters. Native *sql.Tx methods are available only in a Transaction callback.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_client.go-1.txt",
              "quote": "QueryRow(ctx context.Context, dest []interface{}, query string, args ...interface{}) error"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_client.go-1.txt",
              "quote": "Get(ctx context.Context, dest interface{}, query string, args ...interface{}) error"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_client.go-222.txt",
              "quote": "TxFunc func(*sql.Tx) error"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "claim": "Client.Get/Select use sqlx struct scanning. Default NameMapper lowercases Go field names; it does not convert CamelCase to snake_case and does not read json tags. Explicit db tags must match selected columns (or deliberate projection aliases). Do not disable strict mapping to hide a mismatch.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "local_path": "sources/jmoiron_sqlx-sqlx.go-18.txt",
              "quote": "var NameMapper = strings.ToLower"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/jmoiron_sqlx-sqlx.go-18.txt",
              "quote": "reflectx.NewMapperFunc(\"db\", NameMapper)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
