      ],
      "provides_symbols": [],
      "semantic_links": [
        {
          "claim": "Transaction callbacks receive a native *sql.Tx. Operations in that callback return native SQL/driver errors, not the framework errors expected by IsDupEntryError. The helper only accepts *errs.Error. Classify native driver errors in the callback or use framework helpers on the normalized error returned by Client.Transaction.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_client.go-222.txt",
              "quote": "TxFunc func(*sql.Tx) error"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_error.go-1.txt",
              "quote": "e, ok := err.(*errs.Error)"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_transport.go-101.txt",
              "quote": "return errs.New(int(mySQLError.Number), mySQLError.Message)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "claim": "A non-nil callback error causes rollback, then RoundTrip normalizes the returned error. An arbitrary callback sentinel/custom error can become a framework network error with its message, losing original identity/type. Preserve domain classification as local callback state instead of testing custom error identity after Transaction. This is a source-derived middleware interpretation, not a business implementation.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_transport.go-268.txt",
              "quote": "if err := req.tx(tx); err != nil {"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_transport.go-61.txt",
              "quote": "err = generateTRPCError(err)"
            },
            {
              "local_path": "sources/mysql-mysql_transport.go-101.txt",
              "quote": "return errs.NewFrameError(errs.RetClientNetErr, err.Error())"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
